Database migrations (Alembic)
=============================

Alembic owns the PostgreSQL schema in production. Locally and in tests the
app still calls `Base.metadata.create_all()` (init_db), which builds the full
current schema on a fresh SQLite DB — so day-to-day dev needs no migrations.

The connection URL comes from the `DATABASE_URL` env var (see alembic/env.py),
so every command below assumes it is set (or falls back to local SQLite).

Common commands
---------------
    alembic upgrade head        # apply all pending migrations
    alembic current             # show the DB's current revision
    alembic history             # list the revision chain
    alembic downgrade -1        # revert the last migration

Creating a new migration
-------------------------
    alembic revision -m "add telemetry table"      # hand-written
    alembic revision --autogenerate -m "..."       # diff models vs DB

Always review autogenerated migrations before committing.

Deploying to Render
-------------------
Run migrations before the app boots so it never queries columns that don't
exist yet. Set the service's **Pre-Deploy Command** to:

    alembic upgrade head

(Render injects DATABASE_URL automatically, so no manual DB access is needed.)
Alternatively, prepend it to the Start Command:

    alembic upgrade head && uvicorn app.main:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port $PORT

The existing production table is picked up safely: 0001_baseline skips the
CREATE when `contacts` already exists, then 0002 adds the new columns and the
unique constraint (removing any duplicate passes first).
